<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════ §05 -->
<section id="s-context" data-code="context">
<div class="section-no">05 — Effective Context Length</div>
<h2>Claimed vs Actual: The RULER Benchmark</h2>

<p>
  "128k context window" has become a marketing number. The <strong>RULER benchmark</strong> tests whether a model
  can actually <em>use</em> its context — retrieving specific facts buried in long documents, following multi-hop
  references, tracking variable values. A score below 85.6 is considered "not effectively using that length."
</p>

<p>
  The results are stark. Select a model below to see its RULER score curve:
</p>

<div class="vp">
  <div class="vp-head">
    <span class="vp-title">RULER Score vs Context Length</span>
    <span class="vp-hint">threshold 85.6 = effective use</span>
  </div>
  <div class="vp-body">
    <div class="viz-btns" id="ruler-btns">
      <button class="viz-btn active" data-model="lfm">LFM-3B (32k)</button>
      <button class="viz-btn" data-model="llama">Llama 3.2 3B (128k)</button>
      <button class="viz-btn" data-model="gemma">Gemma 2 2B (8k)</button>
      <button class="viz-btn" data-model="phi">Phi-3.5 3.8B (128k)</button>
      <button class="viz-btn active" data-model="all">All</button>
    </div>
    <canvas id="ruler-canvas" style="width:100%;height:260px;border-radius:6px"></canvas>
  </div>
</div>

<p>
  Llama 3.2 3B <em>claims</em> 128k context but its RULER score drops to 74.1 at 32k — below the usable threshold.
  Gemma 2 2B effectively collapses at 8k (score 0.6). Phi-3.5 3.8B actually achieves usable 32k despite being
  a transformer, but requires 18.4% more parameters than LFM-3B to do so. LFM-3B maintains scores above 89.5
  across its full claimed 32k window.
</p>

<table class="results-table" style="margin-top:1.25rem">
  <thead><tr><th>Model</th><th>Claimed</th><th>Effective (RULER ≥85.6)</th><th>Score @ 32k</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
